From: t00mietum <73576036+t00mietum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:28:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wayfire: lock the screen when idle

The session never locked on its own. Start swayidle and have it run
lxqt-leave --lockscreen after an hour idle, which is when Wayfire's
screensaver starts by default. lxqt-leave runs whatever locker LXQt's
session settings name, so the idle lock and the lock key agree.

lxqt-session already locks before sleep, so swayidle isn't given a
before-sleep command, which would lock twice.
---
 configurations/lxqt-wayfire.ini | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configurations/lxqt-wayfire.ini b/configurations/lxqt-wayfire.ini
index 51b77f369ae79a28bf1fdbe70ad5eb405b40fbea..c252c984413bbad0afa5d5cd3b7607e653fb8893 100644
--- a/configurations/lxqt-wayfire.ini
+++ b/configurations/lxqt-wayfire.ini
@@ -148,7 +148,10 @@ session = lxqt-session && killall wayfire
 # Idle configuration
 # https://github.com/swaywm/swayidle
 # https://github.com/swaywm/swaylock
-# idle = swayidle before-sleep swaylock
+# Lock the screen after an hour idle, which is also when Wayfire's screensaver
+# starts by default. lxqt-leave runs the locker set in LXQt's session
+# settings. lxqt-session locks before sleep on its own.
+idle = swayidle timeout 3600 'lxqt-leave --lockscreen'
 
 # XDG desktop portal
 # Needed by some GTK applications
